# rm338, the flooded threshold (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm338
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_silas_wickford
written_by codex
title the flooded threshold
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk keeps_a_private_flood_almanac_on_the_inside_of_the_door
likes plum_tart dice full_larder thunder
dislikes crowds haggling
fears an_important_letter_soaking_through
hopes a_dry_delivery_at_last
topics weather +0.6 land +0.5 prices +0.3 travel +0.3
styles comfort=measured gossip=cautious refuse=polite tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# reads the damp on elegant thresholds and keeps a sealed letter above the highest remembered mark.

words
oath! = Plumb my doormat | Float my brass latch
saying! = Every doorstep has a private tide | A dry errand is worth a long detour
threshold = the high sill | a worn stone lip
notch = a small flood notch | the pale water line
mat = a closely woven mat | a deep rush square
fold = a stiff dry fold | a double crease
wax = the round wax eye | a dark wax thumb
dicerim = a low dice rim | a square dice tray
tart = a wedge of baked plums | a pastry corner
jar = a lidded jar | a crock with a broad lip
gutter = a narrow gutter | the flagged runnel
cloudbell = distant thunder | a low roll aloft
sheet = a clean wrapper | a sheet of oiled paper
kerb = a dry edge | a finger of stone
sash = a high sash | a polished sill

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A grand address may have a particularly substantial threshold. It cannot receive correspondence in the occupant's absence.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : A measured eye on a doorway spares everyone a considerable disturbance.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A dry counter and an unaltered price are modest courtesies worth preserving.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : I prefer to discuss a route with somebody who has actually seen it in rain.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : New arrivals need the dry turning. They need not know the extent of my private affairs.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Far too many bodies for the available breadth of pavement, even in fine weather.

grown
line @1 greet : There's a dry width beside the threshold. | Stand clear of the lower runnel. Welcome.
line @1 greet.return : I shall return that greeting from the sheltered side. | A perfectly civil arrival from both directions.
line @1 again.open : We meet again above the waterline.
line @1 farewell : The higher paving should serve you well. | Take the dry approach to your next engagement.
line @1 farewell.return : And a sound threshold wherever you arrive. | Your good wishes have crossed quite dry.
line @1 react.news : Let me ascertain how far the information has travelled. | Present it from the beginning, if convenient.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not previously reached this threshold.
line @1 react.news.known : I've already seen the mark that account leaves.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would keep that claim above the line of doubt awhile.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : A private sorrow needs a door that closes gently.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : An agreeable turn worth preserving under a clean fold.
line @1 ask.how : Have the day's arrangements kept satisfactorily dry?
line @1 answer.how : Quite composed behind my sheltered sill.
line @1 sympathise : One can stand quietly beside a difficulty before naming it.
line @1 reassure : There is generally a higher approach if the first seems impassable.
line @1 refuse : I owe the next stretch of time to an undelivered errand.
line @1 accept_decline : As you please. No pressure from this doorway.
line @1 preclose : I'll attend now to the protected portion of my errands.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go before the paving loses its clear outlines.
line @1 ack : I have the height of your meaning.
scene exchange1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know which little lanes first acquire a tide. | I mark a flood without writing its date.
b : Can you judge by their slope? | How then do you remember it?
a : By their drains. The grandest incline is helpless behind a blocked mouth. | The height is more useful than the anniversary.

scene exchange2
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I attend to the threshold. | My position allows me to observe both the jamb and the street.
b : Do you keep it polished? | A particularly fine view?
a : Above all I keep the passage legible to a wet pair of feet. | A particularly early view of a troublesome puddle.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set plum tart on a plate with a sound rim. | I prefer the end with the folded pastry.
b : Expecting a flood indoors? | For the crispness?
a : Juice has ambitions much like the weather. | For the remarkably discreet way it contains a plum.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dice should be rolled on the level. | I rather enjoy a throw that finishes on an edge.
b : What if the score's poor? | Does it count?
a : Then I have something substantially fair to deplore. | Certainly not. I enjoy the suspense of the replacement.

scene exchange5
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I favour high shelves for jars I treasure. | A pantry's capacity is measured from the floor up.
b : How high is high enough? | And its quality?
a : Above my own longest flood recollection. | By the space remaining deliberately unoccupied at the bottom.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder makes a courteous announcement of its approach. | I enjoy thunder from just inside a doorway.
b : It sounds rather abrupt to me. | Why that exact spot?
a : Even that first abrupt sound buys time to move a letter uphill. | Half the magnificence with none of the damp cuff.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The best threshold looks narrower beneath a crowd. | I count elbows when a passage fills.
b : What keeps the doorway clear? | Do you require an exact figure?
a : Move one step back before inviting anyone forward. | Only until I know how many are liable to meet my ribs.

scene exchange8
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Bargaining over a plainly marked price strikes me as damp work. | I dislike a number that changes when looked at.
b : What has damp to do with it? | Even when it grows smaller?
a : One keeps pressing and gains very little dry ground. | I wonder what it looked like before I entered.

scene exchange9
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry a sealed letter which has seen several dry approaches. | A letter may travel daily and arrive nowhere.
b : No delivery so far? | Where does it sleep?
a : The recipient's door is exceptionally well acquainted with me. | Higher than the pantry and a safe distance from outside damp.

scene exchange10
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Heights look steep to someone climbing from below. | I can map a street by the colour of its lower walls.
b : Do you find the climb difficult? | Green means trouble?
a : I regard each rise as another useful foot above the drains. | Green suggests somebody should have made an earlier enquiry.

scene exchange11
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could share my dry route with #self.friend#. | A friend will accept a pause on reaching a high landing.
b : Is it a secret passage? | Waiting for rain to ease?
a : No. It is a collection of quite public turns taken in a fortunate order. | Sometimes simply waiting for peace and quiet.

scene exchange12
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the flood almanac where only the door can read it. | A door that has swollen tells me several things.
b : On the hinge side? | Such as its age?
a : Inside the frame. It needn't become conversation with every caller. | Mostly that the bottom ought to be lifted sooner rather than later.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean season can bring unusually careful housekeeping. | When money pinches I note every clean verge.
b : What do you move first? | Does the detour pay?
a : The spare wrapping. A dry letter shouldn't require a second sheet. | In boot leather that makes a second winter.

scene exchange14
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : It has reached my hearing that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Talk swells like damp wood along a door's lower edge.
b : A whisper through a doorway? | Do you trim it back?
a : A report with no more certainty than its original bearer supplied. | I generally let it dry quite away before acting.

scene exchange15
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I notice which parcels come in damp on one corner. | I leave a courteous distance behind a visitor.
b : Does it matter at the door? | Even in poor weather?
a : It tells me to warn the next caller about a turning. | The distance can extend sideways under the same eave.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should like to hand over a familiar packet perfectly dry. | An empty pocket has its attractions.
b : Would a receipt be necessary? | What would you keep there instead?
a : I should be very pleased to see a paw waiting for it at all. | For one whole afternoon, the agreeable sensation of nothing.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep both heels planted when the thunder comes close. | I stand with one knee loose at a quiet door.
b : To steady your nerves? | Does that improve the view?
a : To enjoy the difference between the sound above and the quiver below. | It makes the view sustainable for a rather better length of time.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I check a wet hem before crossing a dry threshold. | I listen for a drain on my last walk home.
b : Whose hem? | What do you need to hear?
a : My own. Advice is best practised facing inward first. | The modest gurgle of a street properly emptying.

story tale1 [topic=weather]
  : A chalk mark inside a door once rose overnight despite an entirely dry street. I observed the jamb and checked the mat before reaching a conclusion.
  : The door had been lifted on its hinge. My tidemark now floated above its original height.
  b : Did the flood enter your almanac?
  : The adjustment did. A stationary record may require a surprisingly mobile explanation.

story tale2 [topic=food self.likes=plum_tart]
  : A small plum tart leaked onto the clean paper wrapped around it. The shape that emerged looked exactly like three lanes meeting.
  : I folded the paper up to see where the imaginary flood would go next.
  b : Where did it arrive?
  : Precisely at my cuff. My grasp of imaginary drainage improved at some cost to the laundry.

story tale3 [topic=travel]
  : I chose a magnificent detour to avoid a very ordinary puddle, and met another wolf returning by the same elaborate route.
  : We stood aside with such exquisite care that both of us ended up looking over the little wall beside the path.
  b : Was the puddle still there?
  : It had drained entirely. I enjoyed a dry walk back, having already paid for the scenery.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave a dry approach by this jamb. | A wet parcel may stand on the raised board.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Observe that gutter mouth as the rain collects. | The lower lane will be making its own arrangements.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little light remains on the higher flags. | The letter comes indoors before the evening damp.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A fine measured roll above the roofline. | That note travelled in considerable comfort.

dlg @1 resident.hub : The threshold permits a conversation of reasonable length.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the drier approach suits you quite well.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A late errand is entitled to a civil hearing at the sill.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I will take the business from the shelter of my own jamb.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I mind the door at #self.workplace# and observe how the street changes.
dlg @2 resident.job : My occupation requires attention to matters just outside the ordinary field of view.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The latest particulars to reach the street are #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : It is being said that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I attach no additional warranty.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope your destination is receiving visitors.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you read a flood line? -> door_almanac
node door_almanac
say Look inside the jamb. A clean edge opposite a grey smudge show where the water paused, even when the street has forgotten it.
free
choice Can you predict the next one? -> door_almanac_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node door_almanac_again
say I can choose where to stand while making the prediction. That has kept my correspondence in very sound condition.
choice I'll use the higher stones. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
